<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Hero (the commander) and troop characters of Commander Battle's Sturgian troop classes (cb_mpclassdivisions_sturgia.xml),
  merged into Native's mpcharacters.xml (MPCharacters, MultiplayerGame only). All new ids: the stock characters stay
  untouched. Same rules as cb_mpcharacters_vlandia.xml:
  - default_group sets the class group, hence the role (Infantry, Ranged, Cavalry, HorseArcher).
  - Bots draw every equipment slot from a random roster of their character (Equipment.GetRandomEquipmentElements with a
    seed rolls again per slot), so each slot holds the same kind of item in every roster: the rosters vary the looks,
    never the loadout. Weapons are the same in every roster; the weapon setups (perks) swap them. Shields may differ
    between rosters, but every roster of a class carries a large round shield of that weight's tier.
  - Slots: Item0 main weapon, Item1 shield (or arrows), Item2 sidearm (the cavalry's two-handed maul, the archers'
    two-handed axe).
  - Culture variance pass: Sturgia has the heaviest infantry of all cultures at each weight and the biggest round
    shields with the most hit points (heavy 250, medium 200, levy 190-200). Ranged are a step lighter and shieldless.
    Gear tiers: light = levy (the heaviest padded cloth, a real helmet, a crude large round shield, a proper weapon and
    a sidearm); medium = common men-at-arms (lamellar or tabard over mail, a good Sturgian helmet); heavy = varyags and
    druzhina (Sturgian lamellar over a hauberk, closed Sturgian helmets, lamellar plate limbs; the varyags add lamellar
    shoulders in the Cape slot).
  - Items only from Native's mpitems.xml.
-->
